6.4 Progress Monitoring and Reporting
The team will use short development iterations during the 10-week project period. Progress will be reviewed regularly against the agreed scope, requirements, milestones and deliverables.
During project reviews, the team will consider:
activities completed;
activities currently in progress;
upcoming activities;
technical blockers;
Agentaus API or integration issues;
retrieval and grounding issues;
identified risks;
testing results; and
changes required for the next iteration.
Prototype demonstrations and stakeholder feedback will be used to progressively validate requirements and refine the system.
Significant issues affecting project delivery will be communicated to the academic supervisor/mentor and sponsor where appropriate.
6.5 Scope and Change Control
Scope control is particularly important because the project must deliver a functional prototype within ten weeks.
Proposed changes will be assessed according to:
relevance to the identified problem;
value to the core Capstone Assistant;
estimated development effort;
technical complexity;
impact on existing functionality;
additional testing requirements; and
impact on the delivery schedule.
Priority will be given to completing the agreed Micro-SaaS functionality before introducing additional features.

