Functionality such as comprehensive task management, advanced scheduling, automated Gantt charts, risk-management workflows, progress prediction, LMS integration and enterprise deployment will remain outside the current project unless formally reconsidered and sufficient time is available.
6.6 AI Governance and Human Oversight
As the system uses Agentaus AI to generate natural-language responses, AI behaviour will form an important part of project governance.
The assistant will operate using a human-in-the-loop approach. AI-generated responses will provide assistance but will not replace formal academic advice, mentor guidance or stakeholder judgement.
The team will apply the following controls:
project-specific information will only be retrieved for authorised users;
relevant retrieved information will be supplied to Agentaus to support grounded responses;
prompts will be controlled and versioned;
insufficient information will trigger fallback behaviour rather than intentional fabrication;
selected AI responses will be evaluated for relevance and grounded accuracy;
hallucination occurrence will be recorded during evaluation;
AI response latency and request failures will be monitored;
unnecessary project or user information will be minimised in monitoring data; and
users will be able to provide simple feedback on AI responses.

