6.7 Issue Escalation
Issues will initially be discussed within the four-member project team.
An issue should be escalated when it:
blocks development of another component;
affects a major project milestone;
requires a significant change to the agreed scope;
creates an access-control or privacy concern;
causes repeated Agentaus API failures;
significantly affects AI response quality;
cannot be resolved within the project team; or
threatens delivery of the MVP within the 10-week timeframe.
The general escalation path will be:
Responsible Team Member → Four-Member Project Team → Academic Supervisor/Mentor → Project Sponsor where relevant
Technical issues will normally be resolved within the team where possible, while academic, scope and sponsor-related issues will be escalated to the appropriate stakeholder.
6.8 Governance Summary
The governance approach provides sufficient control for a four-member team while remaining lightweight enough for a 10-week prototype project. Collaborative decision-making, controlled scope changes, regular progress reviews, stakeholder feedback and clear issue escalation will support project delivery.
